{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Or if it be made known to him.</b> Its sense is 'and it is made known'; or one may say 'and he knew his sin.' Similar is (Proverbs 30:31): ״זרזיר מתנים או תיש״ — as if it said 'the strutting rooster and the he-goat'; so is the opinion of the commentators." "<b>However,</b> the reason it needed to say הודע with a ה and to add the word או, is because the sin-offering pertains to the final ה of the Name, and therefore it says ״שעירת עזים תמימה נקבה״ — a female goat, whole — and that ה brings upon him suffering, to make known to him his sin, so that he remember and bring his offering. And since it is of the וא\"ו, and the וא\"ו is of the ה, therefore it needed to say או, for through this there will be ״ריח ניחוח לה'״ — a sweet savor to HaShem — and the discerning will understand."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:35.850656854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}